hey guys it's vadim with max tech and as  you already know apple broke the tech  side of the internet with the new 14 and  16-inch macbook pros with their  controversial thick boy redesign and of  course the notch that nobody was  expecting but in reality the real  shocker comes down to apple's new m1 pro  and m1 max chips which are blowing the  minds of basically everyone in the  engineering world and the tech space in  general for various different reasons  which i'm gonna dive deep into in this  video which is a hundred percent focused  on these new chips so what i'm gonna do  is explain everything you need to know  about them including how they work and  what makes them so special compared to  any other computer chip on the market so  without further ado let's get right into  the basics the m1 pro chip is basically  a souped-up version of the m1 chip from  last year packing in twice the number of  performance cores and gpu cores while  ditching two of the efficiency cores  giving us a 10 core cpu and 16 core gpu  on the m1 pro and speaking of those  cores the apple tree on twitter who by  the way wrote this wonderful article has  confirmed that the new chips are in fact  based directly on the course from the m1  chip and if that sounds obvious i  previously speculated that apple would  base these cores on the new ones in the  iphone 13s a15 chip since basically all  of those cores are faster across the  board than the cores in the m1 but as  you can see apple rated the m1 pro's gpu  cores at 5.2 teraflops of performance  which is exactly double the performance  of the m1's 2.6 teraflops confirming  that they're the same exact course on  top of that i speculated that apple  would pack in the a15 chips faster  neural engine that can run over 15  trillion operations per second but nope  apple showed that the one in the m1 pro  is using the m1 chip snurl engine with  11 t-flops of performance so this  basically confirms a few of the other  details about the m1 pro and m1 max  chaps we know that they're not built on  the latest five nanometer plus process  node from tsmc it's just the regular  five nanometer and we also know that the  video encoders and decoders are most  likely identical to the ones in the  regular m1 chat but thankfully apple did  toss in some brand new prores encoders  and decoders which is by the way a world  first from apple no other computer on  the market can do this not even the mac  pro with the dedicated afterburner card  since it can only decode prores now  going back to the chip it of course  packs dedicated thunderbolt 4  controllers right inside of the chip  package as well as many other things  like the secure enclave for security an  image signal processor for the webcam  dedicated caches machine learning  accelerators and more but let's go ahead  and dig deeper into the m1 pro chip by  referring to an antex article on this  topic where andre provided a labeled  graphic of the chip itself  here he pointed out that apple is now  using two blocks of slc cache which  serves the entire chip to amplify  bandwidth reduce latency and improve  power efficiency and apparently this new  chip looks like it's using double the  amount of slc cache 32 megabytes  compared to 16 on the m1 chip now as far  as the ram apple is using unified memory  which is making these chips extremely  special so let me explain how it all  works traditional ram that you find in  many x86 based computers is always  separated from the main cpu and gpu  chips which adds extra latency since  data that needs processing has to travel  through electrical circuits in the main  logic board so to perform a graphically  based task the cpu has to copy data to  the ram and then that data gets copied  to the gpu for processing and once it's  finished the data gets copied back to  the ram again and then copied from the  ram to the cpu so that it can do its  part of the processing before repeating  the cycle all over again and again but  with apple's chips the memory is built  directly into the main package with the  cpu and the gpu and since it's unified  memory both the cpu and the gpu can have  access and work on the data at the same  time without having to copy it back and  forth and with greatly reduced latency  since it's all right there in one  package so to make this as simple as  possible imagine that there are two  painters one is called the cpu sitting  over here and one is called the gpu over  here and they have a single canvas in  the middle for them to paint and work on  it they have to hand it back and forth  to basically process and finish up the  painting but with apple's unified memory  the cpu sitting right here and the gpu  is also right here and they're both  painting on the canvas at the same time  so as you can see in this representation  of the m1 pro chip you have a dedicated  ram chip on each side of the m1 pro and  each ram chip also has its own dedicated  128-bit memory bus for that data to  travel through which effectively means  that the m1 pro has a 256-bit memory bus  which allows up to 200 gigabytes per  second of memory bandwidth which is  extremely impressive and based on  andre's calculations this means that the  ram and the m1 pro is most likely lp  ddr5 ram that runs at up to around  6400 megahertz which is much faster than  the 4266 megahertz ram and the original  m1 but making it even better the way  that apple set all of it up means that  the ram operates through 16 channels  eight channels on the left side and  eight on the right side which is  something that's completely unheard of  in the computer space but before i  explain why this is such a huge deal i  wanna ask you guys to hit that subscribe  button below to help us reach a million  subs before the end of the year and be  sure to use the m1 pro promo code to get  20 off on all of our merch including our  new m1 pro max sharpie edition shirt  down in the merch shelf below getting  back to those crazy 16 channels of ram  the beautiful thing is that you get the  full 16 channels regardless of whether  you choose the 16 gigabyte or 32 gig ram  option since both versions still use a  full ram chip on each side of the m1 pro  the difference is in the use of either 8  or 16 gig ram chips but now let me  explain why having 16 channel memory is  so impressive every single cpu that  intel currently sells uses dual channel  memory yes that's two channels compared  to 16 on the m1 pro so this means that  the current 2020 27 inch imac uses dual  channel memory the 2017 imac pro that i  wrote this script on uses quad channel  memory because of the pro grade xeon  chip and our fifteen thousand dollar mac  pro actually uses six channel memory and  to show you why having more channels is  so important here's a chart showing the  photo editing performance using  lightroom classic as you can see the  performance improves based on the number  of memory channels in the system and we  know this for sure because the imac pro  is actually faster than the regular imac  which doesn't make sense because the  regular imac has doubled the amount of  ram and it has faster cpu performance  than the imac pro but because of the  dual channel memory limitation it  actually ends up being slower in this  raw photo exporting test and to explain  this as practically as possible you can  think of a memory channel as a highway  connecting the ram to the cpu with only  two highways there is going to be a lot  of traffic when moving a lot of vehicles  or data back and forth that's why moving  up to four highways or channels on the  imac pro improved performance despite  actually having a slower cpu since it  freed up all of that traffic and then of  course it got even better with the mac  pros 6 channel memory so now you can  understand why having 16 channels on the  m1 pro chip is such a big deal but wait  there's more and get ready for this  because i'm about to blow your mind  everything i just mentioned was for the  base m1 pro chip so now let's venture  into the more expensive m1 max this chip  is much larger as you can see in this  image being roughly 75 bigger than the  m1 pro and three and a half times bigger  than the original m1 chip so what this  m1 max chip does is it basically doubles  up on many of the components found in  the m1 pro  including double the gpu cores to make a  32 core gpu double the slc cache to make  64 megabytes of cash which can be used  by the entire chip  double the number of ram chips as you  can see in this graph four of them and  double the number of memory buses to  support those ram chips making for an  incredible 512-bit memory interface  which gives the chip up to 400 gigabytes  per second of memory bandwidth and the  craziest thing of all is that the number  of memory channels is once again doubled  yes the m1 max ship regardless of the  amount of ram or gpu cores that you pay  for has 32 channel memory now if that  didn't blow your mind i don't know what  else will because what apple has  achieved is literally an engineering  masterpiece since even the latest epic  server chips from amd are still limited  to just 8 memory channels and to put the  final cherry on top because of the  unified memory architecture the ram is  fully accessible by the gpu meaning that  if you bought the model with 64  gigabytes of ram you essentially have up  to 64 gigs of vram for the gpu to make  use of this makes the m1 max the world's  first chip or gpu to come on the market  with more than 48 gigs of accessible  vram beating out nvidia's quadro rtx  8000 gpu which sells for fifty five  hundred dollars by itself but to give  you guys a more realistic comparison the  previous top-of-the-line 16-inch macbook  pro with the 5600m gpu came with only  eight gigs of vram and the current best  gpu in any windows laptop is the 3080  mobile with up to 16 gigs of vram so you  can see why 64 gigs of vram on the m1  max chip is mind blowing so with that  said hopefully you learned something new  about the m1 pro and m1 max chips and if  i just convince you to order one of them  you can find links to the best deals on  the new 14 and 16 inch macbook pros down  in the description below and if you  enjoyed this video go ahead and click  the circle about to subscribe because we  just ordered eight of these to test out  and make videos on so thanks for  watching and we'll see you in the next  video  [Music]
 

